<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kujula Kadphises</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kujula Kadphises was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushan-empire">Kushan Empire</a> in the 1st century CE. Chief of the Kushan branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bactria">Bactria</a>, he united the five Yuezhi chiefdoms and extended his rule south across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a> into Gandhara. His coins, modelled on Roman and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indo-greek-kingdom">Indo-Greek</a> issues, are a main source for his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kujula-kadphises.jpg" alt="Kujula Kadphises" width="320" height="151" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_the_Kushan_king_Kujula_Kadphises.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
